s3_body:
Hi {{first_name}},

A practical question for anyone running ops on a spread-out team: what does it take to keep a benefit like this going?

With Spill, not much. Setup takes hours, people sign up and book on their own, and you see anonymized, aggregate usage to report on. {{price_line}}

Would it help to see the admin side? [Book a short demo]({{demo_url}}).

Best wishes,
{{sender_first_name}}

Hi {{first_name}},

Before adding anything to a facility's week, it's worth asking what it will cost you in time.

With Spill, the answer is very little. Setup takes hours, staff book sessions themselves, often outside their shifts, and nothing goes through supervisors. You get anonymized usage to report on. {{price_line}}

[See the admin side in a 20-minute demo]({{demo_url}}) if that's useful.

Best wishes,
{{sender_first_name}}

s1_body:
Hi {{first_name}},

{{opener}}

One senior researcher leaving for a bigger lab can set an AI roadmap back months. Research with no clear finish line and headlines that say they're about to be automated wear people down, and that rarely gets said out loud to a founder.

Spill is confidential counseling anyone on the team can reach from Slack or Teams, often the same day, for the whole team, founders included. Setup takes hours, and people arrange sessions themselves. If you want the short version, [Spill's page for AI and deep tech companies]({{industry_url}}) has it.

Best wishes,
{{sender_first_name}}

Hi {{first_name}},

{{opener}}

Agencies tend to lose junior talent fastest: senior-level pressure on junior pay, client feedback that overwrites weeks of work, and pitch weeks that never quite end. Year two is often where it turns into churn, and the resignation can be the first a People lead hears of it.

Spill gives everyone at the agency private counseling in one click from Slack or a phone, often the same day, with evening and weekend sessions. Creative directors and account leads get training to support anyone on their team who's struggling. You can see [what that looks like for agencies]({{industry_url}}).

Best wishes,
{{sender_first_name}}

Hi {{first_name}},

{{opener}}

Clients ask for certain people by name, and in an agency those people are the business. On a lean team nobody's workload has a backup, so when one of them burns out after a run of pitches and Friday-afternoon goalpost changes, the gap usually lands on the founder.

Spill gives the whole agency private counseling in one click from Slack or a phone, often the same day, with evening and weekend sessions. Setup takes hours. There's more on [Spill's page for agencies and studios]({{industry_url}}).

Best wishes,
{{sender_first_name}}

