In community development, the hardest part of the work often comes home with staff: a resident facing eviction, a relapse, a family in crisis. Caseloads grow while funding cycles shrink, and HR usually meets that strain once it has become absence or a resignation.

Spill gives every staff member confidential counseling from any phone, often the same day, including support for secondary trauma and grief. Managers of heavy-caseload teams get training too. [Spill's page for community development organizations]({{industry_url}}) explains what staff get.

Best wishes,
{{sender_first_name}}

Hi {{first_name}},

{{opener}}

Community development teams run on thin cover. When a caseworker is out, their residents still need someone, so one absence becomes extra caseload for colleagues who are already stretched, and grant restrictions leave little room for backfill.

Spill gives all staff confidential counseling from any phone, often the same day, at a price built for nonprofit budgets. There's no minimum team size, no procurement saga, and setup takes hours. More on [Spill for community development organizations]({{industry_url}}).

Best wishes,
{{sender_first_name}}

